Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.29,0:21:18.63,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,{\fs42}我们算力优势的第二个来源，是发现\N{\fs32}The second driver of our compute advantage is our rate of discovery
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.63,0:21:20.09,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,{\fs42}算力增效方法的速度。\N{\fs32}of compute multipliers.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.09,0:21:24.09,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,{\fs42}我们关注的是总有效算力，它等于\N{\fs32}We focus on total effective compute, which is the multiplicative product
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.09,0:21:27.84,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,{\fs42}物理算力容量，乘以我们发现的算力增效倍数。\N{\fs32}of physical capacity, times the compute multipliers that we discover.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.09,0:21:32.31,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,{\fs42}每发现一种增效方法，我们的总有效算力池就会扩大。\N{\fs32}Each one we discover makes our pool of total effective compute bigger.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.47,0:21:33.31,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,{\fs42}例如，\N{\fs32}For example,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.31,0:21:37.02,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,{\fs42}假设训练一个达到特定智能水平的模型，需要 100 单位算力。\N{\fs32}say you need 100 units of compute to train a model of a certain intelligence.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.27,0:21:40.82,Bilingual,,0,0,0,,{\fs42}一种能让有效算力达到原来 4 倍的方法，意味着只需 25 单位算力，\N{\fs32}A 4x compute multiplier means you can use 25 units of compute
